  "title": "Erdős Problem #885",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For integer $n\\geq 1$ we define the factor difference set of $n$ by $ D(n) = \\{\\lvert a-b\\rvert : n=ab\\}. $ Is it true that, for every $k\\geq 1$, there exist integers $N_1<\\cdots<N_k$ such that $ \\lvert \\cap_i D(N_i)\\rvert \\geq k? $ ",
